INFO:conv_wf:buffett: 15 rolling 2-year windows
INFO:conv_wf:  buffett: beat SPY in 6/15 windows, mean excess -3.2%

  CONVICTION WALK-FORWARD — rolling 2-year windows vs SPY over the same dates

  screen                 beat SPY   mean excess    median     worst  turnover
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  buffett                    6/15        -3.2%     -3.7%    -17.3%       7%

  `beat SPY` is the number to read. A screen winning in most windows has
  an edge that survives regimes; one winning in half is indistinguishable
  from a coin, however good its full-period CAGR looks.

  These screens have no fitted parameters — Piotroski, Novy-Marx and
  Greenblatt all published before our data begins — so this is not a test
  for overfitting. It is a test for whether one lucky stretch is carrying
  sixteen years.

  Windows overlap, so they are not independent observations. Read the win
  count as a description, not as a significance test.
